NAME
       pvremove - remove the LVM label from a device

SYNOPSIS
       pvremove [-f] [-y] PV...

DESCRIPTION
       pvremove wipes the LVM label from a physical volume, so the device is
       an ordinary disk or partition again. A PV that still belongs to a
       volume group cannot be removed: first move its data away (pvmove) and
       take it out of the VG (vgreduce VG PV), or remove the whole VG
       (vgremove).

OPTIONS
       -f, --force
              Remove even when LVM has doubts. Use -ff to remove a PV that is
              still listed in a VG (this breaks that VG).

       -y, --yes
              Answer yes to the questions.

EXAMPLES
       Take /dev/vdc out of vgdata and free it:

           vgreduce vgdata /dev/vdc
           pvremove /dev/vdc

SEE ALSO
       pvcreate(8), vgreduce(8), pvmove(8), lvm(8)
